<title>PANAMA: Panama Medcom buys country's main cable TV station.</title>
<headline>Panama Medcom buys country's main cable TV station.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panamanian consortium Medcom Holding Inc said on Friday it bought Panama's main cable television company, Cable Onda 90, for $32 million.</p>
<p>Cable Onda 90 has 25,000 subscribers. Medcom already holds the country's two main television channels, RPC Television and Telemetro.</p>
<p>((-- Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
